COMMUNICATIONS SECURITY PROTOCOL -- ALL MEMBERS
Issued under Pain's supreme authority (see pain_supreme_authority.docx)

We are eleven people opposing every hidden village at once. We do not get to be careless
about how we talk to each other. This is not a suggestion.

1. No standing infrastructure beyond what a given operation actually needs. We are not
   a village -- we do not maintain permanent networks, permanent servers, or permanent
   accounts anywhere we don't already control the ground. Anything stood up for an
   operation comes down when the operation ends.

2. Assume every channel is compromised until proven otherwise, and re-assume it after
   any member is captured, killed, or unaccounted for longer than expected.

3. Records exist only where they must. Operation logs, technique files, and financial
   records are kept because Leader requires them for coordination -- not because it is
   convenient. What doesn't need to be written down should not be written down.

4. No personal correspondence through any channel used for organisation business, ever.
   Sasori's puppet-collection habits, Kakuzu's bounty bookkeeping, Deidara's opinions on
   art -- keep it verbal, keep it separate.

5. If you believe your communications have been intercepted, say so immediately. A
   member who stays quiet about a possible compromise to avoid a difficult conversation
   is a bigger liability than the compromise itself.

This is why our footprint looks different from a village's. A village governs people and
keeps records because it has to. We do not, and we do not leave more of ourselves lying
around than an operation strictly requires. That gap is deliberate and it is the reason
we are still eleven and not fewer.

-- filed under Policies & Orders per standing procedure, which is itself the one
concession to record-keeping this protocol makes
